---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { dataUrl } from '../data'
import { repoUrl } from '../site.mjs'

const sql = `select date, onboarded_pibs, raw_power_pibs
from '${dataUrl}/daily_network_metrics.parquet'
order by date desc
limit 7;`
const python = `import polars as pl

df = pl.read_parquet("${dataUrl}/miners.parquet")`
const js = `const url = "${dataUrl}/daily_network_metrics.json"
const rows = await (await fetch(url)).json()`
const db = `attach '${dataUrl}/fdp.duckdb' as fdp (read_only);
use fdp;
show tables;`
const prompt = `Answer my question with Filecoin Data Portal datasets.
Each dataset is a Parquet file at ${dataUrl}/<dataset>.parquet.
Dataset definitions and column descriptions live in ${repoUrl}/tree/main/assets/main.
Query with DuckDB. Read the column descriptions before writing SQL.
Dates are UTC. Null means unknown, not zero. Atto-denominated columns are exact
DECIMAL(38,0) integers; keep them exact and divide by 1e18 only for display.
Show the SQL you ran and the latest date each answer covers.

Question: `
const examples = [
  ['DuckDB', 'DuckDB example', sql, 'Copy SQL'],
  ['Python', 'Python example', python, 'Copy Python'],
  ['JavaScript', 'JavaScript example', js, 'Copy JavaScript'],
  ['Whole database, DuckDB 2.0+', 'Whole database example', db, 'Copy SQL'],
]
---

<Layout title="Docs" description="Query Filecoin Data Portal datasets with SQL, Python, JavaScript, or an agent, and read them correctly.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Docs</h1>
    <p>Every dataset is a Parquet file at a stable URL, rebuilt daily. Query it from anywhere that reads Parquet, and check definitions before drawing conclusions.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="duo">
    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="sql">
      <h2 id="sql">Query the files</h2>
      <p>Each table in the <a href="/datasets">catalog</a> lives at <code>{dataUrl}/&lt;dataset&gt;.parquet</code>. Run SQL in the DuckDB CLI or in the browser with <a href="https://sql-workbench.com/">SQL Workbench</a>. <code>daily_network_metrics</code> is also published as JSON for dashboards.</p>
      {examples.map(([label, aria, code, action]) => (
        <div class="copy">
          <div class="copy-head">
            <span class="meta">{label}</span>
            <button class="button" type="button" data-copy={code} hidden>{action}</button>
          </div>
          <pre tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={aria}><code>{code}</code></pre>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="agent">
      <h2 id="agent">Ask an agent</h2>
      <p>Point a coding agent at <a href="/SKILL.md">SKILL.md</a> or <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>. Every dataset page also has a Markdown version listed in the <a href="/datasets.md">Markdown catalog</a>. Or paste this self-contained prompt and add your question.</p>
      <div class="copy">
        <div class="copy-head">
          <span class="meta">Prompt</span>
          <button class="button" type="button" data-copy={prompt} hidden>Copy prompt</button>
        </div>
        <pre tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Agent prompt"><code>{prompt}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="caveats">
    <h2 id="caveats">Read before citing</h2>
    <ul class="caveats">
      <li>Daily tables end at UTC yesterday at the latest. Sources update on different schedules, so tables can end on different dates.</li>
      <li>Null means unavailable or undefined, not zero. Gaps in a source leave dependent metrics empty.</li>
      <li>Definitions live in column descriptions and asset SQL. A metric name alone is not a definition.</li>
      <li>Atto-denominated columns are exact integers. Keep them exact and divide by 1e18 only for display. Never add amounts in different tokens.</li>
      <li>Filecoin Pay volume covers all rails, not only storage. Warm storage capacity and network power measure different populations; do not divide one by the other.</li>
      <li>Provider checks are synthetic probes, not client traffic or a promise of availability.</li>
      <li>Ratios use pooled counts. Do not average per-provider percentages.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="sources">
    <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
    <p>Datasets come from Lily chain data, Filecoin JSON-RPC, the RIBA FEVM receipt archive, the Filecoin API, ProbeLab Dealbot checks, and market data. Each dataset page lists its sources and links the asset code that declares them. The <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/docs/data-sources.md`}>Filecoin data sources guide</a> compares these and other APIs, indexers, and RPC endpoints, with access details and limits.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="project">
    <h2 id="project">Open source</h2>
    <p>SQL and Python pipelines, dataset definitions, and this site live in <a href={repoUrl}>one repository</a>. Each dataset page links its asset code. Missing a source or a dataset? Corrections and requests are welcome as <a href={`${repoUrl}/issues/new`}>issues</a> or pull requests.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
